    "created_at": "2016-06-15T16:10:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-15T16:10:32Z",
    "body": "@gsnedders was this what you had in mind?\n\nI'm thinking that the naming scheme could include some information like the section, insertion mode, etc, would be more useful.\n\nCurrently the spec auto-generates IDs for each link, e.g.\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#preprocessing-the-input-stream:parse-error\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#preprocessing-the-input-stream:parse-error-2\n\nbut since these are automatically generated when building, they are not stable if the spec moves things around or adds or removes some parse error.\n\nMaybe the IDs should be of the form _section-id_:_link-text_:_short-name_ where the short-name is given with a new attribute in the source? This would require a change to wattsi but I can maybe take a stab at that. This would be useful to give more stable IDs to any xref in the spec, not just parse errors.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
