    "updated_at": "2016-06-15T17:27:44Z",
    "body": "I don't think purely numeric parse error numbers is that useful: it doesn't convey any useful semantic. It'll also end up awkward when we add things to the parser and end up with them out of number.\n\nSo no, @zcorpan, it's not. I was imagining something more like the keys in the E dict at https://github.com/html5lib/html5lib-python/blob/master/html5lib/constants.py#L7. We shouldn't use these directly because they're not all great.\n\n> Maybe the IDs should be of the form _section-id:link-text:short-name_ where the short-name is given with a new attribute in the source? This would require a change to wattsi but I can maybe take a stab at that. This would be useful to give more stable IDs to any xref in the spec, not just parse errors.\n\nThe link text is almost always \"parse error\" so it should probably be section-id:short-name. But I'm not sure we want section-id in there; I'd rather have _error-short-name_. We don't want something too long, IMO. It does still require a change to wattsi, but if you're happy to do that…!\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
